# BP Dumper — Windows Go exe + Python reference

**Shipped Windows product:** `scripts/bp-dumper-go/` → packaged as `DumperApps.exe`
via `scripts/installer/build-exe.ps1` (native Go; no PyInstaller / no UPX).

**Protocol / behavior reference:** `scripts/bp-dumper-py/` (still used for macOS/Linux
and as the behavioral source of truth when changing parse/webhook rules).

| Client | Status | FS discovery |
|---|---|---|
| Native Go Windows exe | **Canonical Windows download** | Drive auto-scan / path prompt OK |
| Standalone Python | Scripts / non-Windows; keep in sync with Go for protocol | Drive auto-scan / path prompt OK |
| Store WinUI (`apps/bp-dumper-store/`) | **Parked** — listing may stay live; do not invest in feature parity | FolderPicker only (legacy sandbox experiment) |

Shared wire notes (for webhook / Edge): `scripts/bp-dumper-shared/PROTOCOL.md`.

## When changing BP Dumper

- Member-facing Windows behavior must work in **`scripts/bp-dumper-go/`**.
- Prefer updating **both** Go and Python when changing log regexes, webhook event
  shapes, wizard keys, update prompts, or path discovery.
- Do **not** require Store WinUI updates for new member features.
- Keep `feat(dumper)` / `fix(dumper)` Conventional Commits for semantic-release.
- Release path triggers on dumper paths (see `release-dumper.yml`); include
  `scripts/bp-dumper-go/**` when shipping Windows binary changes.

## Do not regress

- Auto-detect / drive search is a **wanted** member feature on the Windows exe
  (leave blank in the wizard to search; paste a path to override).
- Do **not** reintroduce GitHub auto-download / self-replace of `DumperApps.exe`
  (AV dropper / Wacatac heuristics). Updates stay manual from GitHub Releases.
- Do not reintroduce PyInstaller `--onefile` for the published `DumperApps.exe`.
- VirusTotal gate stays **0 malicious** — do not allowlist Trojan heuristics.
